      "summary": "Rewriting a whole app in Rust costs months, minute-long compiles and gigabytes of target/. Most of the runtime sits in a few functions anyway. fast-anything finds those functions, has your coding agent port only them to Rust, proves the port gives the same results on real recorded calls, and swaps it in. npm i -g @el4cteo/fast-anything or: cargo install fast-anything Ports are compiled with your Rust toolchain (rustup). fast-anything go --agent claude -- python app.py or: -- node app.ts / bun app.ts / deno run -A app.ts / ruby app.rb / java App.java / mvn exec:java / gradle run / go run .",
